WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.467 --> 00:00:02.734
-Two nights in a row
we're hanging out.

00:00:02.734 --> 00:00:03.901
-I know. You and me, look at us.
-Yeah, look at us.

00:00:03.901 --> 00:00:05.300
-Hey, look at us.
-Look at us.

00:00:05.300 --> 00:00:07.133
I saw you last night at
the premiere of "Sweeney Todd."

00:00:07.133 --> 00:00:09.000
-Yeah.
-And we saw each other

00:00:09.000 --> 00:00:11.133
and said hi and waved,
went over.

00:00:11.133 --> 00:00:12.501
-Little cuddle, yeah.
-What'd you think?

00:00:12.501 --> 00:00:13.801
-Oh, my God.
It was brilliant.

00:00:13.801 --> 00:00:16.400
-Yeah, it's a fantastic play.
It was really great.

00:00:16.400 --> 00:00:18.734
-Really magical.

00:00:18.734 --> 00:00:20.868
-But we were talking
because I was like,

00:00:20.868 --> 00:00:22.601
"You're here.
What are you doing here?"

00:00:22.601 --> 00:00:23.801
You're like --
You moved here.

00:00:23.801 --> 00:00:25.100
-Yeah, yeah, I moved here.

00:00:25.100 --> 00:00:27.334
-You're a New Yorker.
-She's a New Yorker now.

00:00:27.334 --> 00:00:29.567
-I'm happy you're here.
I'm happy you're a New Yorker.

00:00:29.567 --> 00:00:32.534
Are you a -- are you --
Do you people watch?

00:00:32.534 --> 00:00:34.701
Do you, uh...?
-Oh, yeah, obsessively.

00:00:34.701 --> 00:00:36.200
-That's my favorite part.
-It's my favorite part, right?

00:00:36.200 --> 00:00:37.801
-Yeah, everyone's so different.
-Yeah.

00:00:37.801 --> 00:00:39.100
-And also, you know,
I feel like there are

00:00:39.100 --> 00:00:41.334
so many things that you can
only see in New York.

00:00:41.334 --> 00:00:42.968
Like, I don't know.
Have you guys seen this?

00:00:42.968 --> 00:00:45.601
Where it's like someone
will be walking around with,

00:00:45.601 --> 00:00:48.167
like, a snake around their neck?
-Oh, of course, yeah.

00:00:48.167 --> 00:00:50.067
-Right? Yeah. "Oh, that guy."
-Or roller skates or something?

00:00:50.067 --> 00:00:51.300
-Oh, yeah, that guy.
We all know that guy.

00:00:51.300 --> 00:00:52.834
-Yeah, he walks around
with a snake around --

00:00:52.834 --> 00:00:56.300
I know that, dude.
-Snake guy Lemmy -- yeah.

00:00:56.300 --> 00:00:57.601
-Yeah. There's always a guy
walking around

00:00:57.601 --> 00:00:58.868
with a snake around,
and you go, "What's up, dude?"

00:00:58.868 --> 00:00:59.868
-Yeah, yeah.
-That's normal.

00:00:59.868 --> 00:01:01.567
-It's totally normal.
-Oh, yeah.

00:01:01.567 --> 00:01:03.434
-No, I feel like the beautiful
thing about New York is that,

00:01:03.434 --> 00:01:06.200
like, anything goes.
Everything is human,

00:01:06.200 --> 00:01:08.300
and everything's valid,
and it's like every day

00:01:08.300 --> 00:01:11.267
is, you know, like an adventure
into seeing, you know...

00:01:11.267 --> 00:01:13.067
-You said you saw
a guy walking a goat.

00:01:13.067 --> 00:01:15.400
-I've seen numerous people
walking goats.

00:01:15.400 --> 00:01:16.601
[ Laughter ]

00:01:16.601 --> 00:01:19.467
-I've never seen anyone
ever walking a goat.

00:01:19.467 --> 00:01:20.701
-You're like the fourth person
to say that to me,

00:01:20.701 --> 00:01:22.334
and I'm starting to feel
a little weird about it.

00:01:22.334 --> 00:01:23.601
-Do you know
what a goat looks like?

00:01:23.601 --> 00:01:24.968
-It's been different goats.

00:01:24.968 --> 00:01:26.434
-No. Maybe you're
looking at a dog

00:01:26.434 --> 00:01:27.734
and you just don't know
the difference.

00:01:27.734 --> 00:01:28.734
[ Laughter ]

00:01:28.734 --> 00:01:30.033
You go,
"Look at all these goats!

00:01:30.033 --> 00:01:31.968
There's like 30 goats here."
It's a dog park.

00:01:31.968 --> 00:01:34.100
-This new breed of micro dog
with hooves.

00:01:34.100 --> 00:01:35.801
-It's a dog.
-It's taking over.

00:01:35.801 --> 00:01:38.467
-You saw a goat?
-Multiple goats.

00:01:38.467 --> 00:01:41.267
Don't!
Don't gaslight me right now.

00:01:41.267 --> 00:01:42.868
This is very --
[ Laughter ]

00:01:42.868 --> 00:01:45.200
-Were you in the zoo?
-No. This is like --

00:01:45.200 --> 00:01:46.667
[ Laughter ]

00:01:46.667 --> 00:01:48.334
-Maybe you went
to the zoo by mistake.

00:01:48.334 --> 00:01:51.100
-Lower East Side.
-Wow. New York has changed, man.

00:01:51.100 --> 00:01:52.634
Wow.
-That's right. Yeah.

00:01:52.634 --> 00:01:54.868
-Last time you were on our show,
thank you for performing.

00:01:54.868 --> 00:01:56.767
You performed "Boyfriend"
on our show,

00:01:56.767 --> 00:01:59.767
and that was a massive,
massive hit.

00:01:59.767 --> 00:02:02.267
And so congrats, and thanks
for coming on our show

00:02:02.267 --> 00:02:04.133
and doing that.
But I heard that --

00:02:04.133 --> 00:02:06.701
[ Cheers and applause ]
No, it's so good.

00:02:06.701 --> 00:02:08.400
But I heard a story
that that you almost

00:02:08.400 --> 00:02:09.801
didn't release it at all.

00:02:09.801 --> 00:02:11.300
-Yeah. So, "Boyfriend"

00:02:11.300 --> 00:02:13.100
was something that --
that came out of, like --

00:02:13.100 --> 00:02:16.901
I had just done a super small
black-box-theater tour

00:02:16.901 --> 00:02:19.601
where I was just sort of meeting
my fans, traveling around,

00:02:19.601 --> 00:02:21.934
sort of like figuring out
what it means to perform live.

00:02:21.934 --> 00:02:23.934
-Yeah.
-And then we ended.

00:02:23.934 --> 00:02:25.801
My voice was shot.
And the very next day,

00:02:25.801 --> 00:02:26.968
my label was like,

00:02:26.968 --> 00:02:28.567
"You have to start
working on your album."

00:02:28.567 --> 00:02:30.267
So we got into
the studio immediately,

00:02:30.267 --> 00:02:32.133
and we wrote "Boyfriend"
in like two hours,

00:02:32.133 --> 00:02:33.667
and I was like, "This is bad."

00:02:33.667 --> 00:02:36.033
And I recorded it
in like 20 minutes,

00:02:36.033 --> 00:02:37.501
and we just put it away,

00:02:37.501 --> 00:02:39.267
and I didn't really think
anything of it.

00:02:39.267 --> 00:02:41.567
And then -- And then, yeah,
it turned out to be, like,

00:02:41.567 --> 00:02:44.033
the thing that kind of
gave me a sort of

00:02:44.033 --> 00:02:45.334
surprise second career.

00:02:45.334 --> 00:02:47.133
-Yeah, well, did you --
how did you release it?

00:02:47.133 --> 00:02:48.734
Like, did you put it
on TikTok or something?

00:02:48.734 --> 00:02:50.400
-Yeah. So --
So, my label at the time --

00:02:50.400 --> 00:02:51.734
-No, I'm serious.
-Yeah.

00:02:51.734 --> 00:02:53.133
[ Laughter ]

00:02:53.133 --> 00:02:54.801
So, my label at the time said,

00:02:54.801 --> 00:02:56.567
"You know, this is --
this is what people do now.

00:02:56.567 --> 00:02:58.300
You have to let people know
you're making music.

00:02:58.300 --> 00:02:59.701
Would you just do
the due diligence

00:02:59.701 --> 00:03:00.868
and, like, put it on TikTok?"

00:03:00.868 --> 00:03:02.601
And I was like,
"I'm so bad at TikTok.

00:03:02.601 --> 00:03:04.133
Like, you really want me to --"
And so I --

00:03:04.133 --> 00:03:05.801
I threw it up for nine seconds

00:03:05.801 --> 00:03:07.767
or something
and then went to sleep.

00:03:07.767 --> 00:03:09.601
And I woke up the next day
and everybody was like,

00:03:09.601 --> 00:03:11.300
"You have to check your phone."
-Shww!

00:03:11.300 --> 00:03:13.400
-Yeah.
-I mean, it's a smash, pal.

00:03:13.400 --> 00:03:15.100
-Thanks.
-Congratulations.

00:03:15.100 --> 00:03:17.934
And now, of course,
I want you to enjoy this moment,

00:03:17.934 --> 00:03:19.467
but, of course,
everyone's gonna ask,

00:03:19.467 --> 00:03:20.801
"Are you working
on something else?"

00:03:20.801 --> 00:03:22.167
Or you're working
on a new album?

00:03:22.167 --> 00:03:24.934
-Yeah. So, I'm actually
working on my debut album

00:03:24.934 --> 00:03:26.834
pretty much every day now,

00:03:26.834 --> 00:03:28.601
which I'm very,
very excited about.

00:03:28.601 --> 00:03:29.801
-Closer and closer?

00:03:29.801 --> 00:03:32.467
-Yeah. I think
the whole kind of --

00:03:32.467 --> 00:03:34.534
The idea is that you're supposed
to write like a hundred,

00:03:34.534 --> 00:03:37.100
choose your favorite 60,
get it down to the best 40 --

00:03:37.100 --> 00:03:38.467
-What?
-And -- yeah --

00:03:38.467 --> 00:03:40.501
-100 songs?
-And those don't have to be

00:03:40.501 --> 00:03:42.033
songs that you like.
[ Laughter ]

00:03:42.033 --> 00:03:44.033
Which is, like,
actually kind of a task.

00:03:44.033 --> 00:03:45.467
Yeah.
-Holy mackerel.

00:03:45.467 --> 00:03:47.567
So you're write -- How many
songs have you written so far?

00:03:47.567 --> 00:03:49.567
-Oh, I mean,
close to that, definitely.

00:03:49.567 --> 00:03:51.033
-Are you kidding me?
-Yeah.

00:03:51.033 --> 00:03:52.400
-Oh, my gosh.
-You just write every day.

00:03:52.400 --> 00:03:54.133
That's kind of the job
is you just go into the studio

00:03:54.133 --> 00:03:56.634
and you just nose to
the grindstone write every day.

00:03:56.634 --> 00:03:57.767
-What's the last song you did?

00:03:57.767 --> 00:03:59.133
Can you say --
Are you doing with the --

00:03:59.133 --> 00:04:00.501
-I'm not gonna tell you
right now.

00:04:00.501 --> 00:04:02.968
-Come on!
No one's -- no one's listening.

00:04:02.968 --> 00:04:07.734
-I'm only gonna tell them.
You can't know, but we got you.

00:04:07.734 --> 00:04:09.067
-Any special guest stars?

00:04:09.067 --> 00:04:10.701
-Honestly, there will be --

00:04:10.701 --> 00:04:12.501
I think there will be
a few surprise guest stars

00:04:12.501 --> 00:04:14.167
on the album.

00:04:14.167 --> 00:04:16.467
But my next single
that I'm releasing

00:04:16.467 --> 00:04:20.267
is actually going to be a collab
with my good buddy Diplo.

00:04:20.267 --> 00:04:21.801
-No way!
-Yeah.

00:04:21.801 --> 00:04:23.467
[ Cheers and applause ]
-Now we're -- now we're talking.

00:04:23.467 --> 00:04:25.767
-Yeah.
-That's fantastic.

00:04:25.767 --> 00:04:27.567
-Yeah, I'm really excited.
-Last time you were here,

00:04:27.567 --> 00:04:30.734
not only are you a great actor
and singer,

00:04:30.734 --> 00:04:34.767
but I had you do voices of
Minions last time you were here.

00:04:34.767 --> 00:04:38.300
You do an amazing, spot-on
impression of the Minions.

00:04:38.300 --> 00:04:40.701
-Oh, thank you.
-And could you do it again?

00:04:40.701 --> 00:04:42.601
[ Laughter ]
-This -- This --

00:04:42.601 --> 00:04:44.000
This is why you asked me back.
-Yes.

00:04:44.000 --> 00:04:45.567
-Yeah, I know.
-I loved it.

00:04:45.567 --> 00:04:46.801
I won't even look at you.
Just do it.

00:04:46.801 --> 00:04:48.300
-Okay. I can't look --
I can't look at anybody

00:04:48.300 --> 00:04:50.501
while I do it.
-Okay.

00:04:50.501 --> 00:04:52.701
-♪ Baa, baa, baa ♪

00:04:52.701 --> 00:04:55.133
♪ Po-ta-to naa ♪

00:04:55.133 --> 00:04:56.133
[ Laughter ]

00:04:56.133 --> 00:05:01.567
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:05:01.567 --> 00:05:03.234
-I love when you do that.

00:05:03.234 --> 00:05:04.701
Thank you.
Thank you for doing that.

00:05:04.701 --> 00:05:06.534
Is there any other impressions
that you could do on my show?

00:05:06.534 --> 00:05:08.334
-I can probably do only
the impressions

00:05:08.334 --> 00:05:10.100
that sound very akin
to the Minions.

00:05:10.100 --> 00:05:11.567
-Yeah. Like what?
Like what?

00:05:11.567 --> 00:05:13.801
I feel like --
like, a "Toy Story" alien

00:05:13.801 --> 00:05:15.367
is, like,
right in that same lane.

00:05:15.367 --> 00:05:17.033
-Yeah.
-Right? It's like --

00:05:17.033 --> 00:05:18.968
You're gonna say it's the same
because it's the same.

00:05:18.968 --> 00:05:21.667
It's like -- I love this.
Don't look at me.

00:05:21.667 --> 00:05:23.334
-It's like...

00:05:23.334 --> 00:05:25.167
"He has been chosen."
Wait. What is it?

00:05:25.167 --> 00:05:27.367
[ Laughter, cheers, applause ]

00:05:27.367 --> 00:05:29.501
Wait. Yeah.
-Yeah, it is good.

00:05:29.501 --> 00:05:31.534
-"The claw!"
-Oh, wow!

00:05:31.534 --> 00:05:33.100
[ Laughter, cheers, applause ]
-That's really good.

00:05:33.100 --> 00:05:36.234
-Don't do that!
-No, I was in shock, how great.

00:05:36.234 --> 00:05:37.534
-Thanks.
-It sounds like the original.

00:05:37.534 --> 00:05:39.467
-Listen.
You're like my publicist.

00:05:39.467 --> 00:05:40.701
You're gonna get me
really good work out of this.

00:05:40.701 --> 00:05:42.100
-Yeah.
-This is my calling.

00:05:42.100 --> 00:05:44.200
-Yeah.
Let's talk about "Schmigadoon."

00:05:44.200 --> 00:05:45.767
Can we, please?
This is season two.

00:05:45.767 --> 00:05:48.133
You play a different character
than you did last season.

00:05:48.133 --> 00:05:50.234
What's happening
with this season?

00:05:50.234 --> 00:05:52.567
-So, yeah.
So this season,

00:05:52.567 --> 00:05:55.701
for "Schmigadoon,"
our two heroines,

00:05:55.701 --> 00:05:57.434
played by Keegan-Michael Key
and Cecily Strong,

00:05:57.434 --> 00:05:58.801
who are so brilliant.
-They're great.

00:05:58.801 --> 00:06:00.133
Yeah, yeah, yeah.
-Yeah.

00:06:00.133 --> 00:06:02.734
[ Applause ]
Brilliant.

00:06:02.734 --> 00:06:05.300
They have -- They have escaped
the world of Schmigadoon.

00:06:05.300 --> 00:06:07.701
They've returned back
to New York City,

00:06:07.701 --> 00:06:09.767
and they've realized
that they they feel like

00:06:09.767 --> 00:06:11.434
they're missing a little bit
of magic in their life.

00:06:11.434 --> 00:06:14.033
And they both kind of,
at the same time, decide,

00:06:14.033 --> 00:06:15.167
"What if we try to go back

00:06:15.167 --> 00:06:16.601
and we try to get
back into Schmigadoon,

00:06:16.601 --> 00:06:18.534
just for, like, a little
kind of like quick pick-me-up?"

00:06:18.534 --> 00:06:19.934
-Yeah.
-Yeah. You know.

00:06:19.934 --> 00:06:21.868
-Of course.
-Relatable.

00:06:21.868 --> 00:06:23.934
And so they go back into
the woods,

00:06:23.934 --> 00:06:25.567
dressed in Schmigadoon attire,
to kind of

00:06:25.567 --> 00:06:27.300
try to find the magic again.

00:06:27.300 --> 00:06:28.467
And they find themselves

00:06:28.467 --> 00:06:30.901
in a very different
dimension of musicals

00:06:30.901 --> 00:06:35.000
that are much darker,
sort of sexier -- giggling --

00:06:35.000 --> 00:06:38.367
you know, absinthe-filled,
and -- and adventure ensues.

00:06:38.367 --> 00:06:39.734
-Yeah.
I want to show everyone a clip.

00:06:39.734 --> 00:06:42.234
Here's Dove Cameron
in season two of "Schmigadoon."

00:06:42.234 --> 00:06:43.567
Take a look at this.

00:06:43.567 --> 00:06:47.000
-We are going to become
the best of chums.

00:06:47.000 --> 00:06:48.400
I just know it.

00:06:48.400 --> 00:06:49.901
And I have the most
spectacular people instincts.

00:06:49.901 --> 00:06:51.501
I'm quite literally never wrong.

00:06:51.501 --> 00:06:54.467
Madame Frau says that
it's because I'm an old soul.

00:06:54.467 --> 00:06:56.300
And she should know.
I mean, she's practically 50,

00:06:56.300 --> 00:06:57.701
the old battleaxe.

00:06:57.701 --> 00:06:58.868
-50's not that old.

00:06:58.868 --> 00:07:00.434
-How long were you two
planning on staying?

00:07:00.434 --> 00:07:04.000
-I hope it's terribly long.
-Uh, we -- we are --

00:07:04.000 --> 00:07:06.200
No, we -- we are not sure.
-Oh, no!

00:07:06.200 --> 00:07:08.000
But you simply
must stay forever.

00:07:08.000 --> 00:07:09.634
We're going to have the most
marvelous time together,

00:07:09.634 --> 00:07:11.100
the three of us.
In fact,

00:07:11.100 --> 00:07:13.367
you must come to see me perform
at the club tonight.

00:07:13.367 --> 00:07:15.934
I have a brand-new number, and
it's going to be just fabulous.

00:07:15.934 --> 00:07:17.367
And I'll just die
if you don't come.

00:07:17.367 --> 00:07:19.234
Promise me you're going to come.
Swear on your lives.

00:07:19.234 --> 00:07:20.901
-Just say yes.
-Sure, we'll be there.

00:07:20.901 --> 00:07:24.300
-Oh, you are little dears,
the both of you.

00:07:24.300 --> 00:07:26.067
Mwah!
Okay.

00:07:26.067 --> 00:07:27.968
I will see you tonight.

00:07:27.968 --> 00:07:29.534
Au revoir.

00:07:29.534 --> 00:07:30.634
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:07:30.634 --> 00:07:32.234
-Wow. That's how you do it
right there.

00:07:32.234 --> 00:07:34.133
Dove Cameron, everybody!

00:07:34.133 --> 00:07:37.701
"Schmigadoon" premieres
April 5th on Apple TV+.

00:07:37.701 --> 00:07:38.968
We'll be right back

00:07:38.968 --> 00:07:40.133
with more "Tonight Show."
Stick around.

